LeNet-5 ASIC -- block-level stimulus for the two MAC blocks, 2026-08-15
=======================================================================

Filtered evidence log for the tier that gives conv5x5_row_mac and
dense_row_mac a testbench of their own, and re-measures the gate-level
mutation scores that motivated it.

  make sim-mac-conv    tb_conv5x5_row_mac vs golden/quantized_conv.py
  make sim-mac-dense   tb_dense_row_mac   vs golden/quantized_conv.py
  make gls             both netlists, now driven by those testbenches too

Tools: Icarus Verilog 12.0, ModelSim ASE 18.1, Yosys 0.68, Python 3.14.4.
PDK:   /root/OpenROAD-flow-scripts/flow/platforms/sky130hd/lib/
       sky130_fd_sc_hd__tt_025C_1v80.lib

What was filtered: the per-vector transcripts and the yosys per-cell tables.
Kept here are the verdict lines, the mutation campaigns in full, and the
coverage figures each testbench asserts on. Nothing was edited.

Regenerate with:

  make sim-mac-conv sim-mac-dense 2>&1 | tee mac_raw.log
  make gls                        2>&1 | tee gls_raw.log

`make gls` needs the sky130hd liberty from an ORFS install and so does not run
in CI; `make sim-mac-conv` and `make sim-mac-dense` are part of `make
regression` and do.

------------------------------------------------------------------
1. The two new testbenches, RTL
------------------------------------------------------------------
PASS tb_conv5x5_row_mac: 6592/6592 cases matched the Python golden model
  peak +81920 hit 1 times, peak -81280 hit 2 times, 7 cancelled to zero, 2676 negative
  all 5 lanes driven to both -128 and +127

PASS tb_dense_row_mac: 9540/9540 cases matched the Python golden model
  peak +131072 hit 1 times, peak -130048 hit 2 times, 6 cancelled to zero, 3812 negative
  all 8 lanes driven to both -128 and +127

The peaks are the theoretical ones: 5 x 16,384 = 81,920 and 5 x -16,256 =
-81,280 for the 5-tap MAC, 8 x 16,384 = 131,072 and 8 x -16,256 = -130,048 for
the 8-lane one. Each testbench $fatals if it did not reach both, if fewer than
six rows cancelled to zero, or if any single lane was never driven to both int8
extremes.

Under ModelSim ASE 18.1, same vectors:

  # PASS tb_conv5x5_row_mac: 6592/6592 cases matched the Python golden model
  # Errors: 0, Warnings: 0
  # PASS tb_dense_row_mac: 9540/9540 cases matched the Python golden model
  # Errors: 0, Warnings: 0

Full regression afterwards: 26 PASS lines, 14 distinct testbenches, 0 failures.

  14/14 RTL testbenches passed -- full log in results/regression_summary.log

------------------------------------------------------------------
2. RTL mutation campaigns -- proof the testbenches can fail
------------------------------------------------------------------
Mutations are applied to the RTL, the matching testbench is run, and the RTL is
restored. Each campaign runs an unmutated control first, because "all caught" is
also the score of a harness that fails on everything.

A mutation that does not compile is reported INVALID, not CAUGHT. An earlier
version of this harness scored a build break as a catch; the mutation labelled
C-M4 was rewritten in legal Verilog and re-run rather than counted.

== conv5x5_row_mac / tb_conv5x5_row_mac
  control (unmutated): PASS tb_conv5x5_row_mac: 6592/6592 cases matched
  C-M1 drop lane 4 from the tree:              CAUGHT
       MISMATCH [0]: got -3675, expected -3116
  C-M2 lane 2 takes lane 3 weight:             CAUGHT
       MISMATCH [0]: got -3144, expected -3116
  C-M3 zero-extend lane 1 instead of sign-extend: CAUGHT
       MISMATCH [0]: got 62420, expected -3116
  C-M4 tie bit 0 of the row sum low:           CAUGHT
       MISMATCH [2]: got -3088, expected -3087
  C-M5 lane 0 reads lane 1 activation:         CAUGHT
       MISMATCH [0]: got 451, expected -3116
  ---> 5/5

== dense_row_mac / tb_dense_row_mac
  control (unmutated): PASS tb_dense_row_mac: 9540/9540 cases matched
  D-M1 leaf loop stops one lane short:         CAUGHT
       MISMATCH [0]: got x, expected -2667
  D-M2 lane i takes lane i+1 weight:           CAUGHT
       MISMATCH [0]: got -5601, expected -2667
  D-M3 tree adder becomes a subtractor:        CAUGHT
       MISMATCH [0]: got -243, expected -2667
  D-M4 zero-extend every product:              CAUGHT
       MISMATCH [0]: got 259477, expected -2667
  D-M5 tie bit 0 of the sum low:               CAUGHT
       MISMATCH [0]: got -2668, expected -2667
  ---> 5/5

------------------------------------------------------------------
3. The vacuity guards, proven able to fire
------------------------------------------------------------------
Each testbench asserts that every lane was individually driven to both int8
extremes. That guard was tested by narrowing the *generator*, not the RTL.

  Attempt 1: directed lane sweeps stopped two lanes short.
             Result: still PASSES -- and correctly so. 3,000 uniform random
             rows drive every lane to both extremes on their own, so coverage
             really was achieved. The guard reports coverage, not intent.

  Attempt 2: same narrowing, plus the random and whole-row classes clamped to
             +/-100 so nothing re-covers those lanes.
             Result: FATAL: tb_conv5x5_row_mac: only 5/5 lanes saw -128 and
                     4/5 saw +127

