------------------------------------------------------------------
5. Netlist mutation campaigns -- the controlled experiment
------------------------------------------------------------------
Same harness, same five mutations, same netlist, same day. The only variable
between the two runs of each pair is which testbench drives it.

== conv5x5_row_mac / tb_conv5x5_row_mac
  M0-control-unmutated: control PASSES (harness is not stuck failing)
  M1-drop-an-inverter: CAUGHT
  M2-and-becomes-or: CAUGHT
  M3-or-becomes-and: CAUGHT
  M4-tie-an-output-low: CAUGHT
  M5-invert-a-gate-input: CAUGHT
  ---> 5/5

== conv5x5_row_mac / tb_conv5x5_pe
  M0-control-unmutated: control PASSES (harness is not stuck failing)
  M1-drop-an-inverter: CAUGHT
  M2-and-becomes-or: CAUGHT
  M3-or-becomes-and: CAUGHT
  M4-tie-an-output-low: SURVIVED  <-- tier did not catch it
  M5-invert-a-gate-input: CAUGHT
  ---> 4/5

== dense_row_mac / tb_dense_row_mac
  M0-control-unmutated: control PASSES (harness is not stuck failing)
  M1-drop-an-inverter: CAUGHT
  M2-and-becomes-or: CAUGHT
  M3-or-becomes-and: CAUGHT
  M4-tie-an-output-low: CAUGHT
  M5-invert-a-gate-input: CAUGHT
  ---> 5/5

== dense_row_mac / tb_dense_engine
  M0-control-unmutated: control PASSES (harness is not stuck failing)
  M1-drop-an-inverter: CAUGHT
  M2-and-becomes-or: SURVIVED  <-- tier did not catch it
  M3-or-becomes-and: SURVIVED  <-- tier did not catch it
  M4-tie-an-output-low: CAUGHT
  M5-invert-a-gate-input: SURVIVED  <-- tier did not catch it
  ---> 2/5

The 2/5 reproduces results/gls_20260815.log exactly -- same three survivors,
M2, M3 and M5 -- so it is a reproducible property of that stimulus and not a
noisy result. The netlist is byte-for-byte the one that scores 5/5 in the run
directly above it.

The mutation patterns are unchanged from results/gls_20260815.log, deliberately:
changing the harness would have made the before/after incomparable.

  M1  '^  assign _[0-9]+_ = ~[a-z_]'              's/ = ~/ = /'
  M2  '^  assign _[0-9]+_ = .+ & '                's/ & / | /'
  M3  '^  assign _[0-9]+_ = .+ \| '               's/ | / \& /'
  M4  '^  assign [a-z][a-z_0-9]*\[[0-9]+\] = '    's/ = [^;]*;/ = 1'h0;/'
  M5  '^  assign _[0-9]+_ = _[0-9]+_ & _'         's/ \& _/ \& ~_/'

------------------------------------------------------------------
6. Totals
------------------------------------------------------------------
RTL mutations, this tier:            10/10 caught, both controls passing.
Vacuity guards:                      fire on a genuine coverage hole.
gls, each block by its best driver:  22/24 caught, up from 14/19.
gls, all seven campaigns:            28/34 caught.

Remaining survivors, neither closed here:
  avg_pool2x2_int8  M1  a dropped inverter -- caught by make equiv-mapped.
  conv5x5_pe        M3  an OR-to-AND swap in the wrapper logic around the MAC,
                        with no formal cover. A stated gap.
